  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 152 AM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nA weak cold front passage Monday night into Tuesday will bring \na reprieve to the dangerously hot temperatures. Although \ntemperatures will still be hot, temperatures will be around 5 to\n10 degrees cooler than Monday's high temperatures, with sfc \ntemps in the low 90s. Dewpoints will also be slightly cooler as \nwell, keeping heat indicies below any heat headline criteria.\n \nThe \"cooler\" temperatures will continue through the week as the \nupper level ridging becomes focused over the western CONUS, \nkeeping the High Plains in a northwest flow. Friday and Saturday\nwill be the \"coolest\" days of the long term forecast with highs\nmoderating back into the upper 80s across portions of north \ncentral Nebraska into central Nebraska. \n\nThere will also be a series of weak disturbances that move \nthrough the area Tuesday through Thursday, bringing daily \nchances for isolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms. \nConditions will be limited and coverage of storm development \nwill generally remain more isolated to scattered with no \norganized, widespread storm development expected. As for fire \nweather concerns this week, they will remain low despite the \nwarmer temperatures as low level moisture will keep min RH \nvalues around 30 percent or greater.",
